  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Below average temperatures expected today with a \nchance of showers.  \n\nCAMs continues to suggest that a secondary front will push through \nthe Lower Lakes between 14Z-18Z today. This will begin the real push \nof much cooler air in the Lower Lakes with H850 T's falling to 0C to \n-4C by this evening. While the main story will be the chilly fall \nairmass there will be a continued chance of some showers with the \nsecondary front and maybe some lake induce showers. That \nsaid...temperatures will peak in the 50s for the most part, maybe \nsome upper 40s across the higher terrain. It will also be quite \nbreezy with winds gusting up to 35 mph at times.   \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Frost possible in areas tonight. \n\nThe core of the surface based ridge is looking like it will be just \nto our west through tonight. This will 'likely' keep just enough of \na gradient over the Lower Lakes for much of the overnight hours \nuntil very late. Given that...this should limit widespread frost \nacross the area, except for wind sheltered locales. Even so...it \nwould be wise to protect any sensitive plants.\n\nFor Tuesday, after a chilly start it will continue to remain on the \ncool side with temperatures rebounding into the 50s, even cooler \nacross the Tug Hill with upper 40s. Southerly flow develops on the \nwestern flank of the surface high Tuesday night which will induce a \nwarming trend as we head into Wednesday.",
